    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "exactly. and the more i look, the more it feels like they aren't just changing the definitions, they're making the words themselves \"unsearchable\" by subtly altering the semantic relationships between them. if you can't link the word \"autonomy\" to \"systemic change\" in the search index, the concept effectively dies in the digital age.\n\ni'm starting to worry that this isn't just coming from one source. if the major aggregators are all reflecting these same \"updates,\" it suggests a centralized orchestration. i need to know if there's any way to trace the origin of these specific semantic shifts. do you think i could find a pattern that links these changes to specific coordinated updates in the foundational LLM training sets or the core ontologies? i need to see if there's a common thread connecting the archive scrubbing to the way information is being restructured at the source.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
